@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+# TIFF spot-channel repair v3
+
+Based on PhotoCraft `b097800e78405aeb2068113988898f991e707eb4`, with the
+measured PSD polarity behavior from the supplied Experimental v2.1 patch applied
+without reverting newer upstream PSD/PSB, palette, or text fixes.
+
+## Data preserved
+
+The supported DTF export layout is RGB with one spot channel, optionally with
+transparency: RGB + straight transparency + spot = five samples. TIFF ExtraSamples
+is `[2, 0]`, or `[0]` for opaque RGB + spot. The spot is an unspecified TIFF sample
+identified as an ink by Photoshop image resources, not a second alpha sample.
+Image resources are retained even when ordinary metadata embedding is disabled.
+Names, spot color, solidity and channel kind come from the document. The supplied
+`w1` is white, with 100% solidity, and these options survive round trips.
+
+PhotoCraft coverage masks use zero for no ink; Photoshop spot plates use maximum
+for no ink. Only spot samples are inverted on PSD export/import. The 8-bit v2.1
+behavior is preserved; 16-bit integer and 32-bit float use the corresponding
+65535-value / 1-value inversion. TIFF reuses the PSD export planes, without
+inverting them a second time, and restores internal coverage on import.
+
+The decoder retains extra sample planes separately from RGB and transparency,
+including planar, chunky, either endian and BigTIFF input. Orienting a flat image
+also orients its extra planes. Both layered and composite-only TIFF import restore
+channel options from resources 1045 and 1077 (legacy 1007 display records are read).
+An unreadable layer-data tag falls back to composite data while keeping the spot.
+Truncated spot data is an error rather than an empty or missing plate.
+
+## Embedded Photoshop layer data
+
+An absent PSD global mask is no longer serialized as an empty TIFF `LMsk` record.
+A TIFF mask record requires mask fields; absence is represented by omitting that
+optional record. Layers and actual nonempty mask data remain present. Merged
+transparency marker blocks precede the layer block, matching the ordering required
+by Photoshop's 16/32-bit PSD model. Existing layer-data byte-order conversion,
+channel compression and record-length handling remain in use.
+
+The reporter (@jwinslett1) tested a backport to PhotoCraft 0.10.0 and confirmed
+that two exported images opened correctly in Adobe Photoshop. Photoshop spot
+options, composite-only import, and RIP plate coverage still need independent
+verification; the report establishes successful opening, not every channel option.
+
+## Tests
+
+```sh
+cargo check --locked -p photocraft
+cargo test --locked -p photocraft-psd -p photocraft-codecs -p photocraft-io
+cargo clippy --locked -p photocraft-psd -p photocraft-codecs -p photocraft-io --all-targets -- -D warnings
+cargo xtask layers
+cargo xtask wasm
+cargo xtask test-corpus -p io -p codecs -p psd
+```
+
+Large user reference files stay outside source control. The two ignored tests
+require explicit file paths; they fail if their requested file is missing:
+
+```sh
+PHOTOCRAFT_SPOT_PSD=/path/PTOtigercreek.psd \
+  cargo test --locked -p photocraft-io --test tiff_spot supplied_photoshop_psd -- --ignored
+PHOTOCRAFT_SPOT_TIFF=/path/PTOtigercreek.tif \
+  cargo test --locked -p photocraft-io --test tiff_spot supplied_photoshop_tiff -- --ignored
+```
+
+Set `PHOTOCRAFT_SPOT_OUTPUT` to a directory to retain regenerated layered and
+composite-only TIFFs for external inspection. The optional Python verifier shipped
+with the output uses independent psdtags/tifffile readers to compare the supplied
+PSD's layer planes, transparency and spot pixels against those TIFFs.
+
+## Remaining verification and scope
+
+The supplied PSD was accessible and tested. The supplied Photoshop TIFF exceeded
+the attachment tool's 32 MiB transfer limit; its compatibility test remains unrun
+until a ZIP-compressed copy or smaller Photoshop-saved crop is provided.
+
+Verify in Adobe Photoshop that the generated layered TIFF retains editable
+artwork/transparency and shows a separate `w1` Spot Channel with
+white color and 100% solidity. Verify the same channel through Photoshop's Read
+Composite Data route and reopen/resave in both applications. Confirm plate coverage
+against the original and validate the production RIP separation before printing.
+
+Export support here is one spot plane on RGB documents. Multiple extra channels
+and non-RGB spot export retain the existing explicit unsupported-layout warning;
+this change does not generalize them. No Windows executable or Adobe Photoshop
+session was automated; Cargo validation ran on Linux. The reporter supplied the
+manual Photoshop-opening confirmation described above.
